<title>USA: Mid-Peninsula Cupertino merger OK'd.</title>
<headline>Mid-Peninsula Cupertino merger OK'd.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mid-Peninsula Bancorp and Cupertino National Bancorp said shareholders of both companies approved their proposed merger.</p>
<p>The combined company will form the lagest multi-bank holding company in the San Francisco Bay Area, with total assets of close to $600 million.</p>
<p>Shareholders of Cupertino National Bancorp will receive 0.81522 shares of Mid-Peninsula for each Cupertino share they own. The merger is expected to be accretive to shareholders of both companies.</p>
</text>
